* Mipmap the glyph atlas. The detailed path point-samples it, so a page drawn
  much smaller than its glyphs shimmers and reads darker than the text really
  is -- measurably so: swept across fields of view, the same page rendered
  detailed and coarse differ by 8 levels of brightness at 0.03 screen pixels
  per layout pixel and by 0.4 at 0.24. The coarse path sidesteps this rather
  than fixing it, and only for text: page backgrounds and the caret still
  alias.
* Replace logo.png with something cooler
* port over the gleditor code, enable glyph by glyph creation
* document everything
